{"game": "sniper-elite-resistance", "language": "english", "appid": 2169200, "month": "2025-06", "window": 3, "start_date": 1750032000, "end_date": 1750636799, "month_true_total": 115, "quota": 9, "returned": 9, "pulled_at": "2026-10-09 09:03:55 UTC", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "197903557", "author": {"steamid": "76561198017883544", "personaname": "usaj0e", "persona_status": "online", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198017883544/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 1, "playtime_forever": 21840, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 142, "playtime_at_review": 4465, "last_played": 1791425270, "avatar": "4536c3aacae50d830c7a533e3feab8961492348a"}, "language": "english", "review": "Like it as a parallel story-line of the Sniper Elite 5 series. Can start in one and end in the other👍", "timestamp_created": 1750618167, "timestamp_updated": 1750618167, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 1, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.50301206111907959", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1738246187", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "197872406", "author": {"steamid": "76561198126368970", "personaname": "DEUS EX", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198126368970/", "num_games_owned": 186, "num_reviews": 25, "playtime_forever": 954, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 841, "last_played": 1753306603, "avatar": "14a0e43e4ec40a0444703a06fbb416ac5ae12040"}, "language": "english", "review": "Basically SE 5 DLC. Same location, same setting only different main character. Western front is overrated we need a eastern front SE where you either play as a German sniper or Soviet one.", "timestamp_created": 1750593819, "timestamp_updated": 1750593819, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 33, "votes_funny": 3, "weighted_vote_score": "0.612845957279205322", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": false, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1738246187", "reactions": [{"reaction_type": 17, "count": 1}, {"reaction_type": 6, "count": 1}]}, {"recommendationid": "197809664", "author": {"steamid": "76561198894963346", "personaname": "UnHolyXXIV", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/UnHolyXXIV/", "num_games_owned": 1059, "num_reviews": 46, "playtime_forever": 866, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 643, "last_played": 1787445663, "avatar": "d854065fea38508e633d690681b17e5aa1402902"}, "language": "english", "review": "Overview\r\nSniper Elite Resistance is a solid spin-off from the Sniper Elite series, offering a unique blend of stealth, tactical sniping, and resistance warfare set in WWII France. While it’s a more focused and shorter experience compared to the mainline games, it delivers tense gameplay and a decent challenge for fans of tactical shooters.\r\n\r\nWhat Works:\r\nAtmosphere & Setting: The game captures the gritty feel of WWII French resistance, with authentic weapons, environments, and a sense of stealthy sabotage.\r\n\r\nSniping Mechanics: True to the series, the sniping feels rewarding with realistic bullet physics and satisfying kill cams.\r\n\r\nTactical Gameplay: Emphasis on stealth and careful planning, sneaking behind enemy lines to take out targets quietly.\r\n\r\nCo-op Option: Adds fun multiplayer stealth missions with friends.\r\n\r\nWhat Could Be Better:\r\nShorter Campaign: The storyline and content are limited compared to main Sniper Elite titles, making it feel brief.\r\n\r\nAI Behavior: Enemy AI can be inconsistent — sometimes very alert, other times surprisingly lax.\r\n\r\nLimited Variety: Gameplay can become repetitive due to fewer mission types and environments.\r\n\r\nFinal Thoughts:\r\nSniper Elite Resistance is a worthwhile experience for fans of the Sniper Elite series looking for a tighter, stealth-focused WWII game. Its strong sniping mechanics and atmospheric setting shine, though those seeking a deeper or longer campaign might feel a bit shortchanged.\r\n\r\nRating: 7.5/10 — A solid tactical shooter with room to grow.", "timestamp_created": 1750528292, "timestamp_updated": 1750528292, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 1, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.50301206111907959", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": false, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1738246187", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "197766504", "author": {"steamid": "76561199122893924", "personaname": "Mittenz", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/MittenzVR/", "num_games_owned": 156, "num_reviews": 129, "playtime_forever": 500, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 500, "last_played": 1750489455, "avatar": "e8d3b82aaa528bc9b58c5173432aeee5b40830d1"}, "language": "english", "review": "Same thing for every mission. 2 main quests, 1 \"Hit\" quest (2 \"Hits\" in only one mission), and 1-2 optional quests for all 8 missions of the game. The ending is lack luster and really anticlimactic. Every mission it's blowing something up. Overall, I did not have fun playing this game which is really disappointing considering I like the Sniper Elite franchise. If I had to rate it, I would give it a 7/10. The graphics are okay, the cut scenes look like they came from a old xbox game, the guns feel eh, I don't need so much MACH. soft point, or anything that can't kill (I know MATCH can kill but I don't need something to help reduce bullet drop). I will not be playing this game ever again :)", "timestamp_created": 1750490169, "timestamp_updated": 1750490169, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 2, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.504814326763153076", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": t